  "id": "nonconformity",
  "term": "nonconformity",
  "definition": "Nonconformity is being seen as not fitting expected educational norms, such as matching peers, meeting teaching standards, or following school rules. In this context, it is a socially judged difference that can lead adults to view ordinary school diversity as a possible problem or pathology.",
